# Design: Deterministic verification automation (T005)

## Problem
Behavior implementation starts with T009, but AGENTS.md sections 6
and 11 demand repeatable checks first: ordinary tests must need no
credentials, no API spend, and no network.

## Approach
One Vitest runner covers package tests and repository checks; cargo
owns fmt, clippy, and unit tests; one command (npm run check) runs
every gate that CI runs. No new dependency was added.

## Key Trade-offs
- Hand-written structural checks instead of Ajv: the repo rules out
  Ajv for the runtime, and authoritative artifact validation belongs
  to the Rust core anyway. The checks encode documented invariants
  (draft 2020-12, unique $id per file name, additionalProperties
  false on object roots, local $ref resolution), not general
  validation.
- SplitMix64 implemented twice (Rust core, TS support) with shared
  golden values, so cross-language parity is under test without a
  shared fixture file (fixtures arrive in T006).
- Two Vitest configs instead of an environment-variable gate, so the
  live lane works on every shell without cross-env.
- to-do.json validated by a mirror of to-do.schema.json plus two
  semantic rules (unique ids, existing dependencies), because the
  task file changes every iteration.
- research/ is excluded from link and name scans: AGENTS.md keeps
  historical records and quotations with original wording.

## Gotchas
- jq's // operator treats JSON false as absent; use
  .additionalProperties == false in one-off queries.
- V8 rolls impossible dates over (2026-02-30 becomes 03-02), so the
  date check compares the stated day against its month.
- A quoted wrong name form is a quotation, not a use; the scan strips
  double-quoted spans before it matches.

